instruction:
The in-house npm package `csvsum` in /app/csvsum is broken: `npm test` fails, the package cannot be loaded with `require`, and a tarball from `npm pack` does not give a working `csvsum` command.

Fix the package so that:
- `npm test` passes in /app/csvsum (do not edit the files under /app/csvsum/test);
- `require('/app/csvsum')` loads the package and exports `summarize` and `format`;
- a tarball made with `npm pack` from a clean copy of /app/csvsum, installed on its own into another prefix, provides a `csvsum` command that works (`csvsum FILE [COLUMN]`, see the README);
- `csvsum` is installed globally from /app/csvsum with `npm install -g`, so that `csvsum FILE [COLUMN]` works on the PATH from any directory. /data/sales.csv is an example input.

The machine has no network; npm is already configured for offline use.
